<article class="env-lemma" id="0EUB">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0EUB">Lemma <span data-tag="0EUB">35.13.3</span>.</a> Let $\{ f_ i : X_ i \to X\} _{i \in I}$ be a family of morphisms of schemes. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
If the family is universal effective epimorphism in the category of schemes, then $\coprod f_ i$ is surjective. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
If $X$ and $X_ i$ are affine and the family is a universal effective epimorphism in the category of affine schemes, then $\coprod f_ i$ is surjective. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Omitted. Hint: perform base change by $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(\kappa (x)) \to X$ to see that any $x \in X$ has to be in the image. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>